provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist  (The request renames the data field of watchlist items: WatchItem.watched becomes WatchItem.seen, everywhere it appears. Three units are implicated: movie (exports the type), watchlist-store (creates/toggles/persists the field), and watchlist (renders it). Only the field is renamed; API names (toggleWatched, watchedCount), UI text, and the unrelated Movie/Tmdb* interfaces stay unchanged. Other units consume only membership checks (onList/isOnList/count), so they are untouched unless the oracle implicates them.)
round 1: owners movie=ok watchlist-store=ok watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (All remaining errors (three TS2339s in the Watchlist template and the assertion at watchlist.spec.ts:66) are confined to the watchlist unit. Round 1's watchlist submission was rejected only because it updated one existing test that asserts the renamed field; since the request is a global rename of `watched` to `seen`, that test modification is exactly what it calls for. I approve that test change and re-instruct watchlist to apply the rename, now including the test update.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist-store  (The watched→seen rename is complete in production: tsc is green and all owner tests pass. The only red tests are my own acceptance tests for watchlist-store, which construct the store outside an injection context (NG0203) even though its constructor legitimately uses effect(). The test must be fixed, not the code: replace it with a version that creates the store via TestBed.)
round 3: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (tsc is green and all 34 tests pass, including the acceptance tests pinning the seen field contract (items added with seen:false, no watched property, persistence round-trip). The rename is complete.)

